    "expensive_path": "Two things at once. Inside every algorithm, the per-joint calculus (jcalc, the motion-subspace products S and S-transpose, SE3 act and actInv, inertia transforms) is the innermost kernel that the recursions call once per joint per sample, so its cost multiplies by every evaluation the module above makes. Separately, configuration-space operations over large sample sets (integrate, difference, interpolate, randomConfiguration, the exponential and logarithm on SE(3) and SO(3)) are the hot loop of sampling-based planners and of reinforcement-learning replay buffers, where millions of independent configurations are mapped at once.",
    "rationale": "This is the geometry layer: the spatial algebra of Featherstone, the library of joint models with their motion subspaces, and the Lie group structure of the configuration manifold. It is conceptually independent of any particular dynamics algorithm, it has by far the largest dedicated upstream test set in the tree, and it is the one part whose acceleration benefits every other module.",
    "excluded": [
      "the Model and Data containers that hold joints, which are shared infrastructure",
