    ],
    "hazards": [
      "The logarithm on SO(3) and SE(3) has branches near the identity and near a rotation of pi, where the code switches to a Taylor expansion; a port that moves the threshold changes the result in the branch neighbourhood, so a check must either avoid or deliberately target those configurations and say which.",
      "Quaternion sign is a representation choice, not physics: q and -q are the same rotation and must not be compared componentwise without normalising the sign.",
      "randomConfiguration draws from an unseeded stream, so every check must pin its configurations.",
